     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "總理任期與流亡",
      "en": "Premiership and exile"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "俄亥俄州立大學的《Origins》刊文稱，索古於1922年12月出任總理，1924年遭暗殺未遂、身受重傷後辭職。國會圖書館國別研究則寫，他的黨在1924年初的國民議會選舉中大勝，隨後他在財務醜聞與暗殺未遂之後讓位給韋爾拉奇；1924年7月農民支持的叛亂控制地拉那，諾里出任總理，索古逃往南斯拉夫。",
      "en": "Origins, the Ohio State University history magazine, says Zog became premier in December 1922 and resigned in 1924 after surviving an assassination attempt that severely wounded him. The Library of Congress study adds that his party won the early-1924 National Assembly elections, after which he stepped aside for Verlaci amid a financial scandal; by July 1924 a peasant-backed insurgency held Tirana, Noli became prime minister, and Zogu fled to Yugoslavia."
     },
